# Copy to .env. The example documents the NAMES; never commit a value.

NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
HOST=0.0.0.0
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Internal cache / dedupe / abuse key material. Never returned to a caller, never logged.
# MUST be at least 32 bytes: the 15-digit IMEI space is enumerable in seconds, so a short pepper
# does not pseudonymise anything. The process refuses to boot below the floor.
#   generate with:  head -c 48 /dev/urandom | base64
SERVER_PEPPER=

# The paid routes appear ONLY when this is set. Without it the service serves the free offline
# tier, which is a supported mode rather than a degraded one: it costs nothing to run.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://imei:imei@localhost:5432/imei_check?sslmode=disable

# ADR-0007: every check's IMEI is encrypted before it is ever persisted. REQUIRED once
# DATABASE_URL is set -- the process refuses to boot without a valid keyring. Format is
# "<version>:<base64 32-byte key>[,<version>:<base64 32-byte key>...]"; current = highest version.
# Rotate by adding a new highest-numbered entry and keeping the old one until nothing references it.
#   generate a key with:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
IMEI_ENCRYPTION_KEYS=

# Loaded into memory at boot. Replace the seed with an Osmocom import before any real use.
#
# Leave this commented out. The code default is an ABSOLUTE path computed from the module's own
# location (see apps/api/src/config.ts), deliberately resolving the same way whether the process
# starts in apps/api (`npm run dev`, cwd = apps/api under npm workspaces) or in the repo root
# (Docker's `node apps/api/dist/server.js`). A relative default here would break one of the two --
# uncommenting it is safe ONLY if you also make it relative to whichever cwd YOUR setup actually
# uses.
# TAC_SOURCE_FILE=testdata/tac-seed.json

# Where the catalogue YAML lives. Defaults to packages/providers/catalogue.
# PROVIDER_CATALOGUE_DIR=

# Public base URL, used to build the feedback_url an async supplier POSTs its answer back to.
# Wrong here means standard orders are placed and their answers land nowhere.
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com

# --- Provider credentials. Read from the platform secret store in production, never baked into an
# --- image and never committed here.
#
# A provider whose credentials are absent is simply NOT BUILT -- not built-and-broken. Running with
# none is the free tier plus a database, and every deep-check section honestly reports
# unavailable(provider_not_configured) at zero cost.

# imei24 (pro.imei24.com) -- legacy DHRU Fusion (form POST to /api/index.php). The sole supplier
# wired up so far; every POST /v1/deep_checks capability routes through it.
# IMEI24_BASE_URL must be https: -- the request body carries the API key and the IMEI.
# IMEI24_BASE_URL=https://pro.imei24.com
# IMEI24_USERNAME=
# IMEI24_API_KEY=

# Real money leaving the business, independent of billing (which is off). GuardedProvider refuses
# a new imei24 order once today's provider_calls sum crosses this, and the section comes back
# unavailable(spend_cap_reached) rather than a silent overspend.
# IMEI24_DAILY_SPEND_USD=10

# POST /v1/deep_checks' total time budget from request start, placing included, before it hands off
# to inconclusive(awaiting_provider) + a GET /v1/deep_checks/:id poll. Must stay below every
# caller's own timeout.
# DEEP_CHECK_WAIT_MS=10000

# --- Worker intervals (apps/worker). Defaults shown.
# WORKER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=30000
# WORKER_WEBHOOK_INTERVAL_MS=15000
# WORKER_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_MS=21600000
